    "id": "ostia-sst-daily-global",
    "stac_version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "The OSTIA (Operational Sea Surface Temperature and Ice Analysis) system produces daily, gap-free maps of sea surface temperature at 0.05° (~6 km) resolution. OSTIA uses satellite data from infrared and microwave radiometers, combined with in situ observations from drifting and moored buoys. The system employs optimal interpolation to merge these data sources and create a foundation sea surface temperature analysis. This product is specifically optimized for polar regions including the Southern Ocean, with integrated sea ice concentration and quality control flags. OSTIA is widely used for numerical weather prediction, ocean forecasting, and climate monitoring. The dataset provides global coverage with daily updates and includes uncertainty estimates for each grid point.",
